# What does not belong on a public web server.
#
# Vercel serves this repository as it is — there is no build step and nothing
# to filter the output — so anything committed here is a URL somebody can
# open. The GitHub Pages workflow used to delete the first line of this list
# on its way out; moving to Vercel took that safeguard away, so it is written
# down here instead of living inside a job nobody runs any more.

# A self-test that signs up REAL accounts and writes REAL rows in the live
# project. Fine to run locally against your own database, not something to
# leave reachable by anyone with the URL.
verify.html

# The test suites, and the database's schema, policies and operating scripts.
# None of it is secret — what protects the data is row-level security, not
# anybody's ignorance of the schema — but none of it is the website either,
# and grant-staff.sql is not a page.
tools/
supabase/

# Notes, stories and the test tooling's manifest. The manifest matters twice:
# it carries a `build` script, and Vercel runs one when it finds one. There is
# no build step in production, and the fastest way to keep it that way is to
# not ship the file that suggests otherwise.
docs/
user-stories/
package.json
package-lock.json
.github/
